## How to Add a New IDoc (Step-by-Step)

### 1. Create the Module Folder

```
src/modules/new-idoc/
├── dto/
│   └── new-idoc.dto.ts          # Raw IDoc TypeScript interfaces
├── entities/
│   └── new-entity.entity.ts     # TypeORM entity
├── interfaces/
│   └── new-payload.interface.ts  # Typed payload interface
├── new-idoc.module.ts            # NestJS module
├── new-idoc.service.ts           # Domain service (upsert logic)
├── new-mapping.config.ts         # Declarative field mapping
└── new.handler.ts                # IDoc handler
```

### 2. Define the Raw IDoc DTO

Model the SAP IDoc structure as TypeScript interfaces:

```typescript
// dto/new-idoc.dto.ts
export interface NewEdiDc40 {
  MESTYP: string;
  SNDPRN: string;
}

export interface NewIdocSegment {
  FIELD1: string;
  FIELD2: string;
}

export interface NewIdoc {
  EDI_DC40: NewEdiDc40;
  E1SEGMENT: NewIdocSegment;
}

export type NewIdocDto = Record<string, { IDOC: NewIdoc }>;
export const NEW_MESTYP = 'NEWIDOC';
```

### 3. Define the Typed Payload

This is the contract between the handler and the domain service:

```typescript
// interfaces/new-payload.interface.ts
export interface NewPayload {
  site: string;
  code: string;
  erpSource: string;
  description: string | null;
}
```

### 4. Define the Mapping Configuration

Use the declarative `FieldMapping` system to map IDoc segments to payload fields:

```typescript
// new-mapping.config.ts
import { FieldMapping } from '@/common/idoc-mapping';

export const NEW_MAP = {
  ediDc40: [
    { source: 'SNDPRN', target: 'erpSource', transforms: ['erpSource'] },
  ] as Array<FieldMapping>,

  segment: [
    { source: 'FIELD1', target: 'code', transforms: ['trim'] },
    { source: 'FIELD2', target: 'description', transforms: ['nullable'] },
  ] as Array<FieldMapping>,
};
```

**Available transforms:** `trim`, `sapDate`, `sapDateOptional`, `float`, `erpSource`, `nullable`

**Context injection:** Use `{ fromContext: 'site', target: 'site' }` to inject values from parent segments.

### 5. Create the TypeORM Entity

```typescript
// entities/new-entity.entity.ts
@Entity('new_table')
export class NewEntity extends TimeStamp {
  @PrimaryGeneratedColumn({ name: 'id' })
  public id: number;

  @Column({ length: 4, name: 'site', type: 'char' })
  public site: string;

  @Column({ length: 18, name: 'code', type: 'varchar' })
  public code: string;
  // ...
}
```

### 6. Create the Domain Service

```typescript
// new-idoc.service.ts
@Injectable()
export class NewIdocService {
  constructor(
    @InjectRepository(NewEntity)
    private readonly repo: Repository<NewEntity>,
    private readonly customLogger: AppLogger,
  ) {}

  public async upsert(payload: NewPayload): Promise<void> {
    // Upsert by natural key
    let existing = await this.repo.findOne({
      where: { site: payload.site, code: payload.code },
    });

    if (existing) {
      Object.assign(existing, payload);
      await this.repo.save(existing);
    } else {
      await this.repo.save(this.repo.create(payload));
    }
  }
}
```

### 7. Create the Handler

The handler is the bridge between raw IDoc and domain service:

```typescript
// new.handler.ts
@IdocHandler('new-idoc')
@Injectable()
export class NewHandler implements IIdocHandler {
  private readonly metadata: IdocHandlerMetadata = {
    description: 'NEWIDOC handler',
    idocFamily: 'NEWIDOC',
    version: 'v1',
  };

  constructor(
    private readonly newIdocService: NewIdocService,
    private readonly customLogger: AppLogger,
  ) {}

  public canHandle(rawPayload: Record<string, unknown>): boolean {
    return !!extractIdoc(rawPayload as NewIdocDto, NEW_MESTYP);
  }

  public getMetadata(): IdocHandlerMetadata {
    return this.metadata;
  }

  public async process(rawPayload: Record<string, unknown>): Promise<void> {
    const idoc = extractIdoc(rawPayload as NewIdocDto, NEW_MESTYP);
    if (!idoc) return;

    const payload = mapAndMerge<NewPayload>([
      [idoc.EDI_DC40, NEW_MAP.ediDc40],
      [idoc.E1SEGMENT, NEW_MAP.segment],
    ]);

    await this.newIdocService.upsert(payload);
  }
}
```

### 8. Wire the Module

```typescript
// new-idoc.module.ts
@Module({
  imports: [TypeOrmModule.forFeature([NewEntity]), ConfigModule],
  exports: [NewIdocService, NewHandler],
  providers: [NewIdocService, NewHandler],
})
export class NewIdocModule {}
```

### 9. Import Module in DaprModule

Just import the module — the `@IdocHandler()` decorator ensures auto-discovery:

```typescript
// dapr.module.ts
@Module({
  imports: [
    DiscoveryModule,
    // ... existing imports
    NewIdocModule,  // ← add (handler is auto-discovered)
  ],
  providers: [DaprService, IdocHandlerRegistry],
})
export class DaprModule {}
```

No `useFactory`, no handler references in providers — the registry discovers all `@IdocHandler()` classes automatically.

### 10. Add Dapr Binding & Environment Variable

Add the binding config and a `@Post` endpoint in `DaprController`:

```typescript
// dapr.controller.ts
@Post(bindings.bindingNewIdoc)
public async receiveNewIdoc(@Req() request: Request): Promise<string> {
  return this.processIdocEvent(request, 'NEWIDOC');
}
```

### Summary: Files Touched

| # | File | Action |
|---|------|--------|
| 1 | `modules/new-idoc/*` | **Create** — module, service, handler, entities, DTOs |
| 2 | `dapr/dapr.module.ts` | **Edit** — import module (handler auto-discovered) |
| 3 | `dapr/dapr.controller.ts` | **Edit** — add `@Post` endpoint |
| 4 | `.env.dist` | **Edit** — add binding env var |
| 5 | `daprComponents/` | **Edit** — add Dapr component YAML |

**No changes to:** `DaprService`, `IdocHandlerRegistry`, `idoc-mapper.ts`, or any other IDoc module.

