## Mapping Utilities Reference

### `idoc-mapper.ts` (master-data-ingestion)

| Function | Purpose | When to use |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `extractIdoc(record, mestyp)` | Find IDOC body by MESTYP key | Always — first step in `canHandle()` |
| `mapSegment(segment, mappings, ctx)` | Map one segment to payload | Single segment mapping |
| `mapArray(items, mappings, ctx)` | Map array-or-single segment | Repeating segments (E1STPOM, E1MKALM) |
| `mapAndMerge(entries, ctx)` | Map + merge multiple segments | Combine EDI_DC40 + E1MASTM + E1STKOM |
| `normalizeToArray(value)` | Normalize single/array to array | SAP sends 1 item as object, N as array |
| `deriveOperation(msgfn)` | MSGFN → 'c' or 'd' | Determine create vs delete |

### `ConfigurableIdocExtractor` (plant-hierarchy-ingestion)

Used for complex hierarchical IDocs (LOIWCS, LOIRNH) with:
- `SegmentMappingConfig` — nesting graph + field mappings + array handling strategies
- BFS path resolution through nested IDoc structures
- Array pick strategies: `'first'`, `'firstWithProperty'`, `'all'`

